<title>FRANCE: Eight injured at Shell refinery in France.</title>
<headline>Eight injured at Shell refinery in France.</headline>
<dateline>MARSEILLE, France 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eight people were slightly injured on Tuesday by an ammonia leak in a refinery owned by Royal Dutch Shell in the southern town of Berre near Marseille, refinery officials said.</p>
<p>The incident occurred when about a cubic metre of the toxic chemical leaked out of a small reservoir during routine maintenance at about 8.30 a.m. (0630 GMT), they said.</p>
<p>The injured were taken to hospital and the leak was sealed off, they said.</p>
